course: dictionary
lesson: 7134
title: A peninsula
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A peninsula is a piece of land that is almost surrounded by water, but it is joined to a larger piece of land on one side. Think of your thumb: water is on most sides, and the land is where it joins your hand.
explain: Context helps you find the meaning. «Florida is a warm peninsula in the south-east, between the Atlantic Ocean and the Gulf of Mexico.» The clue is that it sits between two bodies of water, so a peninsula is land with water on most sides. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Florida is a warm piece of land almost surrounded by water." It still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Compare it with two other landforms. An island has water all the way round it. An isthmus is a narrow neck of land. A peninsula is wider than an isthmus and joined to the mainland. On a map it looks like land poking out into the sea, and the pointed end is «the tip of the peninsula».
fact: A peninsula is land almost surrounded by water, but joined to a larger piece of land on one side.
fact: «Peninsula» is a noun: one peninsula, two or more peninsulas.
fact: Florida, Italy and Cape York in Australia are all peninsulas.
fact: The Iberian Peninsula is the land of Spain and Portugal.
fact: An island has water all round it, while an isthmus is a narrow neck of land.
exercise: «Florida is a warm peninsula in the south-east, between the Atlantic Ocean and the Gulf of Mexico.» What is a peninsula? | Water almost surrounded by land | A narrow river that runs into the ocean | A tall mountain by the sea | *Land almost surrounded by water but joined to more land on one side
exercise: A peninsula is joined to a larger piece of land. What is different about an island? | It is joined to bigger land on one side | It is always covered in ice | It has no water at all | *It has water all the way round it
exercise: Find and copy the word that names a body of water in «The Strait of Malacca, between the Malay Peninsula and the Indonesian island of Sumatra». | Malay | *Strait | Indonesian | Sumatra
test: «The Iberian Peninsula» is the land of which two countries? | Florida and Australia | *Spain and Portugal | Italy and Greece | Sumatra and Malacca
test: On a map, what do you call the pointed end of a peninsula that reaches into the sea? | The centre | *The tip | The mainland | The harbour
exam: Which of these is named as a peninsula in the lessons? | Sumatra | Atlantic Ocean | *Florida | Strait of Malacca
